  "decision_rule": "Fixed before running. Scores are mean HV over seeds per instance, then equal instance weights. (1) The best fixed cut is the cut_X with the highest development mean. (2) A size-adaptive rule picks, for each instance dimension, the cut with the highest mean on that dimension. Both rules are scored out of sample by leave-one-base-out: the cut(s) are chosen without the held-out base instance and its profiles, then scored on them. The size-adaptive rule is adopted only if its leave-one-base-out advantage over the fixed rule has a base-clustered bootstrap 95% interval above zero; otherwise the best fixed cut is selected. (3) The 600 FE cut is called justified if cut_600 is the best fixed cut or the clustered interval of best fixed cut minus cut_600 includes zero. Comparisons with the scaled-UCB pair, the pair without cut and the individuals are descriptive here; they are decided in the confirmation phase.",
